# AI-Assisted: Claude Code (model: claude-opus-5) - Review routing for the two path classes of
# plan.md's Separation gate (task T004).
#
# Two classes, and a pull request may touch one or the other but never both — .github/workflows/ci.yml
# fails a pull request that mixes them:
#
#   content        src/  public/  scripts/  test/  e2e/
#   configuration  wrangler.jsonc  .github/  docs/
#
# Configuration changes carry the Principle 11 limitation recorded in plan.md: Workers Builds deploys
# whatever the merge commit contains, so a wrangler.jsonc change ships in the same deployment as the
# content in that commit. There is no second pipeline to promote configuration through, so the
# compensating control is review: every configuration path below requires a CODEOWNERS review, and
# GitHub does not count a pull request's own author as an approving reviewer — which is what makes
# the required reviewer a NON-AUTHOR reviewer.
#
# This file is only load-bearing when branch protection on `main` has "Require review from Code
# Owners" enabled (task T006). Enabling it is part of that task's declared desired state.

# Default owner for everything not matched below.
